  "notes": "subsidiary rather than reference: the rows read 'Sample n', but the table's function is to give finer timing for activities that already exist in the main SoA (Table 1 rows 'PK' and 'IG', whose grid cells read 'See Section 1.3.1'), which is the subsidiary definition. Recorded as an interpretation - the literal reference test (are the rows procedures performed on subjects?) reads 'no'. 1 leading label column ('Sample #'), so the first data column is position 2 and data columns run 2-6. The 'Study Cycle', 'Day within Cycle' and 'Collection Time Point' columns were kept as data columns rather than treated as further label columns so that their per-row timing values are preserved as cell values."
 },
